has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node   is a piece of oval shaped  pink tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Portions of fat are dissected to reveal 3 distinct nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0 7cm in largest dimension and having a rubbery consistency  The lymph nodes are entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents   is a 22 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right mastectomy specimen with attached 8 x 6 x 1 7cm axillary tissue  which is marked by a stitch  There is an attached REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nipple  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior is inked black  After removal of the axillary tail  the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm stellate  tan pink lesion in a lower inner quadrant of the specimen  2 0cm from the medial edge of the specimen and 0 5cm from the posterior resection margin and 0 8cm from the nearest anterior resection margin  This stellate area is continuous with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm circumscribed  hard  tan solid area that comes 0 3cm to the nearest posterior margin and is 1 5cm from the nearest anterior resection margin  Superior to that area  there is separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hard stellate tan lesion that is partially bridging to the solid area and is separated from it by 2 5cm  The second stellate lesion is greater than 1 5cm from the nearest resection margin  posterior   The rest of the breast tissue is tan  lobular with fat containing focal areas of hemorrhage in the lateral aspect there is a 0 5cm ill defined cavity with smooth surface and slight green discoloration  It is 1 8cm from the nearest posterior resection margin  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the medial most stellate lesion including the anterior and the posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the solid area lateral to the first stellate lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the second stellate lesion including a section towards the nearest posterior resection margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of the ill defined cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of the breast away from the lesions  The axillary tail is dissected from lymph nodes and potential lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph nodes  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  RIGHT   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SEVERAL SMALL FOCI   1 MM   IN ONE NODE AND A SUBCAPSULAR FOCUS APPROXIMATELY 3 MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN A SECOND NODE  MORE TUMOR IS SEEN ON THE DEEPER SECTIONS THAN ON FIRST SECTION   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY  , Positive.
