gative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast tissue  with an accompanying x ray is a 3 x 2 x 1 4cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a wire not in the tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 4cm in widest diameter  firm white brown stellate lesion with ill defined borders  abutting one inked resection margin  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen for ERPR  A section is taken for BRDU analysis  Remainder of tissue submitted in cassettes  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  E  with the lesion in cassettes A through D  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Positive.
