Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 31 CLINICAL DATA  48 year old female with infiltrating ductal carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  1    LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SEE NOTE  2   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  1  In areas the tumor has a tubular pattern  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma is within 0 1cm of the inked superior resection margin  The tumor is 0 9cm in greatest dimension no lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  The single focus of LCIS  slide M  is 0 3cm from a superior margin  NOTE  2  The focus of lobular carcinoma in situ is within 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 20 01 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in three separately labeled parts  Labeled  left  breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue with 2 attached sutures  a long one designating the lateral aspect and a short one designating the superior aspect  The superior portion is inked green  Sectioning reveals firm  white tan  focally  red and gritty  irregular breast parenchyma extending to the inked margins  A representative section of the firm area 1 5cm from lateral edge is frozen as FX 1  Another firm area  1cm in diameterm  0 1cm from the inked margin  lies adjacent to the short suture is frozen as FX 2  The FX 2 is sent to Cox 5  SECTION CODE  A M  entire breast parenchyma  from superior portion to inferior portion  N  FX 1  lateral margin  Labeled  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tan  focally yellow  focally cystic  irregular  cut surfaces  submitted entirely in O through S  Labeled  left axillary contents   is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing several lymph nodes  ranging in largest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  The larger ones have whitish tan solid cut surface  Representative half of each lymph node is submitted in T and U  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT LATERAL  BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA    TUBULAR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  2 SPECIMENS  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 51 CLINICAL DATA  Abundant calcifications on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  THREE FOCI OF MINIMALLY INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 05 CM  REMOVED_DATE CM  AND REMOVED_DATE CM MAXIMUM DIMENSION ON TISSUE SECTIONS   SEE NOTE  2  WIDESPREAD DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING INTO MANY LOBULES AND AREAS OF SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND PRESENT AT MULTIPLE RESECTION MARGINS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The entire specimen has been submitted for histological evaluation  No definite lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is demonstrated  Estrogen and progesterone receptor stains will be performed on sections of one of the larger foci of invasion  slide C  and the results reported as an addendum  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 43 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE INFILTRATING TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE INFILTRATING TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tissue with focal areas of gritty calcification  An accompanying specimen xray show abundant calcifications  A representative section of the gritty  calcified tissue is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder submitted in B R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , Negative.
