tions of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 03     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 19     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Left breast mass  A inferior density  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm red and yellow  focally firm breast tissue fragments  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan  firm lesion with retracted borders focally abutting the inked margin  Representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through G  with the lesion in A through D  Labeled  Posterior breast  calcification  B  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm red and yellow  focally firm breast fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  white material measuring R