ictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 4 x 3 x 0 5cm circumscribed breast fragment with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse  Sectioning into the tissue shows a 0 5cm in diameter  ill defined  firm  tan gray nodule abutting the superficial and deep surfaces  away from the medial and lateral surfaces  The nodule and surrounding tissue is submitted entirely in A through C  the remainder of the tissue entirely in D through I  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION  SMALL NODULE  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT WIDE EXCISION   report_end  , Positive.
