rozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lesion  1  right breast medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with localizing wire in place and accompanying mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm lesion in greatest diameter directly adjacent to the inked margin  Representative section was frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through J  The suspicious lesion submitted in D  E  and F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Inferior right breast tissue   2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with localizing wire in place and accompanying mammogram  The specimen was inked and sectioned to reveal no suspicious areas  Submitted entirely in K through Q  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MEDIAL  1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS INFERIOR  2 LESION   NO SUSPICIOUS AREAS SEEN  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D       