E     REMOVED_CASE_ID     left breast  left  modified radical mastectomy  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  5 9cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect  and long suture designating the lateral aspect  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 10 6cm  tan white skin ellipse is remarkable for a centrally located  mildly retracted  nipple areolar complex  with no additional visible skin changes  The anterior  margin is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The specimen is serially  sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm stellate  irregular  firm tan white  mass that appears centered subjacent to the nipple and extends throughout most  of the breast  The lateral aspect of the mass is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  4 0cm area of tan white fleshy change containing a ribbon shaped metal clip   An additional potential biopsy site is identified approximately 1 0cm medial to  the metal clip  The mass is located a closest distance of  0 1cm to the black  inked posterior margin  0 3cm to the closest blue inked anterior margin  3 5cm  from the medial most aspect of the specimen  7 0cm from the lateral most aspect  of the specimen  3 5cm to the superior most aspect of the specimen  and 0 3cm  to the inferior most aspect of the specimen  The remaining tissue consists of  fat and dense gray white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional masses or  lesions are identified  Multiple intact candidate lymph nodes are palpated in  the lateral tissue  The following representative sections are submitted     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from lateral fleshy nodule within the large mass   to include area containing the clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and closest black inked posterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of mass  submitted from lateral to  medial  to include possible biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   closest blue inked anterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and mass to areolar skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 intact candidate lymph node  bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact candidate lymph nodes each    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable breast parenchyma lateral to the mass     Additional sections were subsequently submitted as follows    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of tumor to areolar skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to lateral  grossly uninvolved skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact candidate lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary fat with potential lymph nodes     Immunohistochemical and in situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts  General Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics  determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of  Pathology at Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or  approved by the U S Food and Drug Administration  FDA   the FDA has determined  that such clearance or approval is not necessary       PART   BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  LEFT       report_end  , Positive.
