acteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in four parts  Labeled  hot spot level I 170 lymph node  are four small lymph nodes ranging from 0 4cm to 0 9cm in greatest diameter  entirely frozen as FX  1 and submitted as A  Labeled  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow tan fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen which is marked by a short  superior  and a long  lateral  stitches  The specimen is inked green  anterior  and black  posterior  and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white tan  firm  stellate lesion within the medial inferior quadrant of the specimen and is 0 5cm away from the closest posterior margin  All other margins are at least 1 0cm away from the mass  The entire specimen is submitted as radial sections as follows  B  Medial  C  Lateral  D  Inferior  E  Superior  F G  Posterior  H I  Anterior  Labeled  right final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of yellow tan  fibrofatty fragments  entirely inked in black and submitted as J and K  Labeled  right medial deep margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow tan  fibrofatty fragment that is inked in black  bisected and entirely submitted as L and M  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Frozen section diagnosis  1 Lymph nodes  right hot and blue level 1 node   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross diagnosis  1 Breast  right   ALL MARGINS ARE GROSSLY NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  SOUHAD YOUNES  MD O R  Diagnosis 