Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 30 CLINICAL DATA  Thickening on exam and density on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS INCLUDING MANY AT ALL MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  NOTE  There is no evidence of blood vessel invasion  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  previously cut into fragment of breast  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm ill defined  firm white lobulated area with focal cystic changes extending within 1 2cm of the medial surface  0 8cm of the anterior surface and 0 1cm of the posterior surface  The superior and lateral surfaces appear away from the lesion  The medial margin is frozen as frozen section  1  resubmitted in A  the inferior margin is frozen as frozen section  2  resubmitted in B  The anterior margin is frozen as frozen section  3 and resubmitted in C  The posterior margin is frozen as frozen section  4 and resubmitted in D  Two radial sections of anterior margin in E  inferoposterior sections in F through H  posterior surface radial section in I  and other sections in J and K  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 1  BREAST  MEDIAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 2  BREAST  INFERIOR MARGIN   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS PRESENT AT THE MARGIN  FOCALLY  SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 3  BREAST  ANTERIOR   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS PRESENT WITHIN CLOSE PROXIMITY OF INKED RESECTION MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS FX 4  BREAST  POSTERIOR MARGIN   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  