ea is serially sectioned to reveal a smooth biopsy cavity inner wall with focal areas of yellowish white discoloration in the wall of the cavity  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  These areas extend to within 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is composed mainly of adipose tissue with focal areas of ill defined white  firm tissue  The nipple and overlying skin is grossly unremarkable  no axillary tail accompanies the specimen  SECTION CODE  A E  representative sections of the cavity  from the region of the stitch with deep resection margin F J  representative sections of nodular areas from the upper outer quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a simple mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm which includes an ellipse of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  with a nipple  Grossly the skin and nipple appear unremarkable  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal multiple areas of ill defined  firm  whitish  tan nodules  The largest measuring 4 0cm in greatest dimension and extends to within 0 3cm of the deepest resection margin  In focal areas there are multiple cysts in the nodular areas  SECTION CODE K T  representative sections of the nodular areas U  representative section of the nipple  Resident  KWAN KEITH  NO ADDRESS                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Positive.
