Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 26 CLINICAL DATA  History of left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1 INFILATRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  20   WITH PAGETOID SPREAD AND EXTENSIVE CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  2 INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  80   MIXED SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  3 ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4 SIMPLE INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The invasive tumor measures approximately 1 0cm in greatest dimension on histologic section and is present at multiple inked resection margins  No definitive vascular or lymphactic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 25                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm that abuts the inked margin  No frozen section done  submitted entirely in A through H  with nodule in A  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SMALL FIRM NODULE TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Katharine Treadway  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
