zen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Left breast   is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gm  26 x 23 x 4cm breast with a 13 x 6 x 1cm axillary tail  Overlying the breast is a 25 x 18cm skin ellipse with a 1cm in diameter  nonretracted nipple  No scars are identifiable on the surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned  A 1cm in diameter  soft  focally firm  tan focally yellow  hemorrhagic area is present at the deep aspect of the breast  corresponding to the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse  This region may represent a biopsy site  Further sectioning through the breast reveals a 5cm diameter  firm  scirrhous  focally gritty  white focally tan and hemorrhagic region at the central superior aspect of the breast  corresponding to the superior aspect of the skin ellipse  The scirrhous tissue approaches to within 1cm of the overlying deep inked surface  Away from the area of the tumor  the breast parenchyma displays prominent fibrous bands interspersed with unremarkable adipose tissue  The axillary tail is dissected and numerous soft to firm  tan to brown nodules are identified  the largest 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative tissue of each is submitted  SECTION CODE  A   nipple B     biopsy cavity  lateral C through G   tumor with overlying inked surface  F and G are contiguous sections   C contains inked deep surface 1 0cm  from tumor  H through J   breast away from tumor  from lateral to medial K through P   representative of each lymph node  Separately received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and designated  Right breast material   are two plastic bags containing a 730 gm  30 x 20 x 3cm aggregate of fragments of breast  The largest fragment is 14 x 11 x 3cm and contains an overlying 15 x 8cm unremarkable skin ellipse  The smallest fragment is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  Also received in the same container is a 12 x 5cm sheet of unremarkable  wrinkled  tan gray pink skin  The breast is sectioned